          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Experimental Study",
          "bbox": [
            59.03,
            68.11,
            161.78,
            80.07
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "TeXGyreTermesX-Bold"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            11.96
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "In our study [Dj23], our objective was to identify the factors driving cognitive fit at a",
          "bbox": [
            41.1,
            91.43,
            398.27,
            101.49
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "TeXGyreTermesX-Regular"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            10.06
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "detailed level. To achieve this, we extended previous research that primarily compared",
          "bbox": [
            41.1,
            103.38,
            398.27,
            113.44
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "TeXGyreTermesX-Regular"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            10.06
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "types of representations by also considering the manner in which information is presented,",
          "bbox": [
            41.1,
            115.43,
            399.51,
            125.37
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "TeXGyreTermesX-Regular"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            9.94
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "contrasting fast-and-frugal decision models with the more conventional expanded ones.",
          "bbox": [
            41.1,
            127.29,
            400.01,
            137.35
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "TeXGyreTermesX-Regular"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            10.06
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Furthermore, we investigated the impact of color highlighting as a key visual factor that can",
          "bbox": [
            41.1,
            139.4,
            398.27,
            149.26
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "TeXGyreTermesX-Regular"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            9.86
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "significantly improve the understanding of these models. To examine the effects of these",
          "bbox": [
            41.1,
            151.2,
            398.27,
            161.26
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "TeXGyreTermesX-Regular"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            10.06
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "elements, we test three hypotheses centered on the effectiveness of decision models grounded",
          "bbox": [
            41.1,
            163.31,
            398.27,
            173.17
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "TeXGyreTermesX-Regular"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            9.86
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "in cognitive analysis of visual search. The formulated hypotheses were tested through a",
          "bbox": [
            41.1,
            175.11,
            398.27,
            185.17
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "TeXGyreTermesX-Regular"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            10.06
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "controlled experiment complemented by an explorative eye-tracking study. The controlled",
          "bbox": [
            41.1,
            187.15,
            398.26,
            197.1
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "TeXGyreTermesX-Regular"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            9.96
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "experiment employed a within-subject design, incorporating three factors: representation",
          "bbox": [
            41.1,
            199.05,
            398.27,
            209.08
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "TeXGyreTermesX-Regular"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            10.03
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "type, representation structure, and representation design. Example decision tables can be",
          "bbox": [
            41.1,
            211.0,
            398.27,
            221.03
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "TeXGyreTermesX-Regular"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            10.03
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "seen in Figure 1. The experiment involved 32 comprehension questions. A total of 139",
          "bbox": [
            41.1,
            222.93,
            398.27,
            232.99
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "TeXGyreTermesX-Regular"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            10.06
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "participants, recruited via Prolific, participated in our study. The results corroborate our",
          "bbox": [
            41.1,
            234.89,
            398.43,
            244.95
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "TeXGyreTermesX-Regular"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            10.06
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "hypotheses: decision tables lead to higher comprehension accuracy than decision trees;",
          "bbox": [
            41.1,
            246.84,
            399.09,
            256.9
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "TeXGyreTermesX-Regular"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            10.06
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "frugal representations are more effective than expanded ones; and using color enhances",
          "bbox": [
            41.1,
            258.8,
            398.27,
            268.86
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "TeXGyreTermesX-Regular"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            10.06
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "comprehension accuracy for decision trees, while it appears to decrease it for decision tables.",
          "bbox": [
            41.1,
            270.9,
            400.01,
            280.77
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "TeXGyreTermesX-Regular"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            9.86
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Our eye-tracking study indicates that this decrease might be attributed to distraction.",
          "bbox": [
            41.1,
            282.78,
